From 1736d4ef7a4fb8cd75811a26789d08908ad0032a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FK-16 candidate <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:42:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] FK-16 (0.3.32 candidate 3): gate checks the packed
 artifact and refuses non-registry copies; evidence fixes

From the independent review of 9f13291:
- B1: linked and file: upstream copies are failures ("not a registry copy"), never skipped.
- B2: the gate packs @feltdb/feltkit from the tree, inspects the tarball (version, FK-16 content, commit,
  only release manifests may differ), probes with the tarball's own contract, and reports its sha512.
- One capability contract: startProbeAuthority + missingPerAgentMethods (runtime/authority-contract.ts),
  used by the gate and by local-authority/policies tests (no more source-text detection).
- Scope registries that differ from the reported registry are refused.
- A failed local start refuses as lasting (no "try again"); an empty authority-url variable is no address
  everywhere; authorityMode is null when nothing was evaluated; every refusal FeltKit makes is recorded.
- authorityMode optional in the exported type; AuthorityMode exported; LOCAL-AUTHORITY.md shipped.
- Docs state each record's actual durability; GUARANTEES decide row no longer says "always the executor".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HaRh2AeLLCdd3FVn7atuCR
